# From the copy that was bootstrap/examples/ruleb-provider-unbound.moss (removed; its
# oracle verdicts are the old Rocq oracle's, historical):
# Rule B (AUDIT-CHANGES #60) at a provider bind: `bind h = g;` uses g,
# which assumes T, with T not in force.
# Audit: rejects (FPDefined). Oracle: rejects ("binding to `g` needs `T` in
# force here"); before #60 it accepted. Native: accepts (exit 0; needs rule B).
# Rule B: binding `g` as a provider is a use of it, so it needs `T` in
# force too.

type T;
fn h();
assume T { fn g() {} }
fn main() { bind h = g; h(); }
